        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Pacman in Perl/Tk]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[In Pacman in Perl/Tk, Alex goes back to a project he worked on in 2013 in order to analyse the separation of logical state from visual representation. By implementing the maze as a two-dimensional array where the shifting and collision functions use tile coordinates instead of canvas pixels, the article is able to exhibit a surprisingly elegant architecture similar to the Model-View approach using standard Perl and Tk.]]></description>
            <pubDate>2026.08.12</pubDate>
            <guid isPermaLink="false">https://blogs.perl.org/users/alex1/2026/08/pacman-in-perltk.html</guid>
            <link>https://blogs.perl.org/users/alex1/2026/08/pacman-in-perltk.html</link>
            
            
            
            <author><![CDATA[alex1]]></author>
            
                
            
            
        </item>
        
